{"text": "BACKGROUND\n\ngrew up ona small farm and | know the\nvalue and results of hard work and\nsacrifice. | had the unfortunate experience\nof losing both of my parents at very\nyoung ages, and | know what it\u2019s like to\neel desperate and alone. | relied on\nstudent loans to help get myself through\nschool and from this | have become a\nstrong advocate for fairness.\nwholeheartedly believe in the ideals of\nour Country and the continuous need to\nstrive to meet them. | believe in the U.S.\nConstitution and the freedoms it bestows\nand | believe everyone deserves respect\nand the assumption of being good. | work\nhard, and play harder, and | have the\nextreme ability to find good in the most\n\ntroubled of situations.\n\nCONTACT\n\nPHONE:\n774-293-8472\n\nWEBSITE:\nTracyforCongress.com\n\nEMAIL:\ntracy@tracyforcongress.com\n\nPILLARS\n\nC-ountry\nL-eadership\nA-ccomplishment\nS-acrifice\nS-ervice\n\nTRACY LYN LOVVORN\n\nRepublican Candidate\nMA- Congressional District 2\n\nWife, Mother, Healthcare Provider, Operational Manager, Small\nBusiness Owner, Advocate, Outdoor/Nature /Animal Lover\n\nEDUCATION\n\nDoctor of Physical Therapy University Of Montana, Missoula, MT\nJan 2020 \u2014 Current\nMaster of Physical Therapy Mount St. Mary\u2019s University, Los Angeles\nAug. 1995 \u2014 Dec. 1997\nB.S. Exercise Physiology / Kinesiology San Diego State Univ.\nAug. 1991 \u2014 June 1995\n\nEXPERIENCE\n\n2018 Republican Candidate MA- Congressional District 2.\nAs a political outsider and relative unknown, | won the Republican Primary\nearning 61% of the vote. As a moderate fiscally conservative republican, |\nran the most successful and cost-effective campaign of all MA\ncongressional republican candidates, receiving 33% of the vote while\nbeing outspent 37-1 by a 22yr incumbent.\n\nCEO Evolution Therapeutics, LLC North Grafton, MA\nOwner operator Evolution Physical Therapy, Outpatient Orthopedics.\nAfter my case settled, (see below) | was in essence black balled from my\nindustry making it extremely difficult to find a comparable job in my field. |\nbecame a practicing clinician again and worked throughout Worcester\nCounty providing physical therapy to individuals in their homes. | then\nopened my own Private Practice Clinic, in my current hometown, and |\nhave been loving every minute of providing care to my local community\never since.\n\nRegional Rehab Director/Manager Clinical, Operations, & Medicare\nCompliance\n20+ years working and growing professionally in the Skilled Nursing and\nRehabilitation environment with various companies across the United\nStates. Professional career path from staff clinician to corporate level\nclinical, operational, and compliance management\n\nSIGNIFICANT ACHIEVEMENTS\n\n2009-2014 *United States ex rel. Lovvorn v. EHSI, ef. al. C.A. 10-1580 (E.D.\nPa) Working in support of the Office of the Inspector General, AG Holder,\nDept of Health and Human Services, and Assistant USAG office of PA, |\nstood up for thousands of sick, elderly, and frail senior citizens in multiple\nskilled nursing facilities. | worked to fight corruption, waste, fraud and\nabuse. My case set a precedent that has worked to SAVE tax payers\u2019\nmoney and has resulted in 100\u2019s of millions of dollars being returned to the\nMedicare Trust Fund. It also forced a change in the methods that rehab is\nbilled in the skilled nursing environment, protecting patients and helping to\nensure quality care.\n\nHold PT License in the States of: MA, MD, PA, NC, CA\nCertified Federal Medicare Surveyor- AAASF Certification\nCHC- Certification in Healthcare Compliance\nIAABO- Certified Official (International Association of Approved Basketball\nOfficials)",
